                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8c81f638-03b5-4590-811d-a99acaa1d9c1",
                        "entry_id": "fe7063ad-8c07-316a-90c8-8787ebe61b9d",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "fairplay"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ee00a9d0-a802-35f9-bb39-580f241ccf71",
                        "entry_id": "fe7063ad-8c07-316a-90c8-8787ebe61b9d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Conduite respectueuse des règles et de l’adversaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Anglicism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c794e34a-0c04-436f-a30d-b07f5d703006",
                                "sense_id": "ee00a9d0-a802-35f9-bb39-580f241ccf71",
                                "text": "Le chartisme aime assez le fair play en Angleterre, ou sera toujours prêt à lui rendre sa partie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "95e638f1-79a6-44e4-a79a-164e08f38c89",
                                "sense_id": "ee00a9d0-a802-35f9-bb39-580f241ccf71",
                                "text": "— Maintenant, ajouta-t-il, tâchez d’être un peu « fair play » et n’oubliez pas qu’il convient toujours de prendre le parti de ses ennemis, à condition qu’ils perdent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1d872490-c3a1-4e12-ad2b-5e38557d1264",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe7063ad-8c07-316a-90c8-8787ebe61b9d",
                        "source_sense_id": "ee00a9d0-a802-35f9-bb39-580f241ccf71",
                        "target_lang_word": "fair play",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fair play",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba3eb93c-6f30-3d44-8e96-4047663a37e2",
                                        "entry_id": "3a09a0d7-f633-3ce1-a379-e2404dafdff5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Good behavior; conduct (in sports or another endeavor) that is respectful of the rules, the spirit of the activity, and the adversary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57eb4e2d-4348-4d08-87f7-af173b6320db",
                                                "sense_id": "ba3eb93c-6f30-3d44-8e96-4047663a37e2",
                                                "text": "The result, eventually, was the conviction of Mr. Hiss on charges of perjury. But the feature that especially appealed to me was the reputation that Congressman Nixon had achieved for fairness in the investigating process. Not once had he overstepped the limits prescribed by the American sense of fair play or American rules applying to such investigations. He did not persecute or defame."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e546a61-2de3-4582-b382-61c9eb59f1a5",
                                                "sense_id": "ba3eb93c-6f30-3d44-8e96-4047663a37e2",
                                                "text": "Financial fair play – talked about as if it is somehow nothing to do with the way the club is run, an imposition upon their work rather than a consequence of the way they work – meant that they could not spend what they do not generate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fair play",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfe3960e-8ad5-3f8f-ae5f-bd1269191a82",
                                        "entry_id": "677957da-be67-36d5-b4ed-ddd7f130556e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "used to acknowledge or congratulate for something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK",
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dce602c6-9e13-4283-81e4-19290e877cbc",
                                                "sense_id": "dfe3960e-8ad5-3f8f-ae5f-bd1269191a82",
                                                "text": "[S]he consolidated her position by purchasing the kennels, doing them up regardless of expense and buying two new horses, and, fair play to her, fair play, as they say in Wales, ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2c61e3f-5250-4e21-ab65-3ade37179a62",
                                                "sense_id": "dfe3960e-8ad5-3f8f-ae5f-bd1269191a82",
                                                "text": "\"Fair play to Jean, he has made it work for him.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b81500b-2f2d-4615-a105-c4c9c19319b5",
                                                "sense_id": "dfe3960e-8ad5-3f8f-ae5f-bd1269191a82",
                                                "text": "The Gaelic Athletic Association, fair play to them, want absolutely nothing to do whatsoever with that thingumajig football tournament in America."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e4db23b-0f69-45fc-8759-d5924ea2f27a",
                                                "sense_id": "dfe3960e-8ad5-3f8f-ae5f-bd1269191a82",
                                                "text": "I wasn't expecting much of Ms Dynamite at the start of the night, but fair play to her, she's got a great voice on her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "183d8c90-de42-4d2b-8013-913e301ff4b2",
                                                "sense_id": "dfe3960e-8ad5-3f8f-ae5f-bd1269191a82",
                                                "text": "Liam Watson: \"Fair play to Southport, they were the best team on paper because they got the most points. We just want to prove we are as good as them\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a3f53fc6-ec22-4151-be3e-5475e998a668",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe7063ad-8c07-316a-90c8-8787ebe61b9d",
